Author: Dimitrios S. Kanakoglou [aut, cre],
    Nikolas Mumm [aut]
Maintainer: Dimitrios S. Kanakoglou <dimkan@dtu.dk>
Description: Builds and compares static predicted interaction neighbourhoods
    around caller-supplied isoform seed sets. Core functionality includes
    virtual pulldown simulations, directional seed-neighbourhood comparisons,
    connected component analysis, and gene set enrichment and
    over-representation analysis (GSEA/ORA) on network topology statistics.
    Statistical seed derivation remains upstream of the package. Annotated
    nonsense-mediated and non-stop decay transcripts are excluded by default
    from protein-network analysis, with explicit inclusion options.
    Developed as part of a master's thesis at the Technical University
    of Denmark (DTU).
